<title>ZAMBIA: ZCCM copper output up 21 pct in May vs Apr.</title>
<headline>ZCCM copper output up 21 pct in May vs Apr.</headline>
<dateline>LUSAKA 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Zambia Consolidated Copper Mines (ZCCM) copper production rose by about 21 percent to 25,801 tonnes in May from 21,380 tonnes in April, central bank figures obtained on Wednesday showed.</p>
<p>The central bank put cobalt production at 340 tonnes from 306 tonnes the previous month.</p>
<p>Copper and cobalt exports rose to 28,496 tonnes and 816 tonnes respectively, from 22,677 tonnes and 471 tonnes in April.</p>
</text>
